dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.audio.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.audio
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION audio wave: REAL binary pack frame,
# replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s old
# `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly, via the proven
# BARE `segment <name> <type>` form: consecutive bare segment lines auto-merge into one segment),
# then `sample_rate` (real fixed `u32` LE) and `audio_format` (real fixed `u8` tag) are genuinely,
# fully described. Past that, `channels` (a homogeneous variable-length collection of per-channel
# variable-length `f32` sample buffers) and `tags` (a homogeneous variable-length collection of
# key/value pairs) are modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain — the `protocol-array-of-
# records` gap: `repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field",
# for an untagged homogeneous record. The real Rust `encode_audio_snapshot_binary`/
# `decode_audio_snapshot_binary` (`../../🦀️.rs`) stays genuinely, fully structured (varint
# counts, real 4-byte LE `f32` samples, per-string length-prefixes) — round-trip tested
# independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))
segment sample_rate u32
segment audio_format u8

chain payload bytes
